  "title": "Velocity across the motion",
  "spoken": "Transverse velocity has the same denominator and an additional gamma.",
  "explanation": "Even a velocity at right angles to the motion changes, because the two systems' clocks run at different rates and are set differently along x.",
  "review": "draft",
  "notation": "modern-pedagogical",
  "unitSystem": "si",
  "assumptions": [
    "The moving system moves along x at speed v relative to the stationary system, with |v| < c; the object's velocity in the stationary system has components along x and y.",
    "Modern teaching notation: gamma is the paper's beta, c its V. The paper composes speeds the other way round, from the moving system to the stationary one; this is the same relation inverted."
